        "desc": "A leucrotta can mimic the voice of a man, woman, child, or a domestic animal in pain. This is often used to lure a victim into attack range. To mimic a voice, the leucrotta must make a Cha (Deception) check opposed by the passive Wis (Perception) of any listeners. Characters who expressly try to determine whether the sound is mimicry can make an active Wis (Perception) check instead."
